8. Sign-in and usage information

Released Binaries use licensebox.dev to verify access to their features.
Sign-in records your verified email address, stated purpose, accepted
terms version, installation public key, operating system, architecture
and app version. Access requests include the modules requested and the
note you supply; the product's administrators receive and answer them.

Machine recognition also uses a product-specific hash derived locally
from operating-system or firmware identity. Raw system identifiers are
not transmitted. The hash binds the installation and its offline lease
to that machine and is retained by the licensing service. Where location
restrictions are configured, the service checks the connection's
approximate IP location when authorizing access.

When usage collection is enabled, the Binaries report command names,
success and failure counts, durations, app version and operating system,
associated with your signed-in account and installation. Usage reports
exclude file names, arguments and geometry. Counts are queued locally
and sent with a later licence check; signing out discards queued counts.

